			<div class="content" id="post-content-4596162">
									

<hr />
<div style="text-align: center;">
<p><span style="color: green"><em>Sippin' on my bubble tea</em></span><br />
<span style="color: blue"><em>Oh I was catching up with my homies</em></span><br />
<span style="color: red"><em>Aw no when suddenly she stood next to me</em></span><br />
<span style="color: green"><em>I couldn't help myself with this shorty</em></span></p>
<p><span style="color: blue"><em>I said I just wanna kick it, sit back and just chill with</em></span><br />
<span style="color: red"><em>You and me we just get along</em></span><br />
<span style="color: green"><em>It's low-key passion, mutual attraction</em></span><br />
<span style="color: blue"><em>Baby you and me we just get along</em></span></p>
</div>
<hr />
<p>Thanks to: ROUNDERHOUSE, AbsentmindedNihilist, MalyceGraves, Sevatar, Popsioak, DrMoned and Crusty_Jon.</p>
<p>Images used are from Wikicommons, found <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Variations_of_Taiwanese_tapioca_pearls.JPG">here</a>,<a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cassava_root_(4626690699).jpg">here</a>, <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kerala_Cassava_plant_2.jpg">and here.</a></p>
<p>I've always hated tapioca. I'm very much a texture-eater, and those little baubles have always looked and felt like slimy little alien eggs to me. My partner, however, loves them, and always makes a point to noisily slurp her bubble tea around me. You can guess what inspired this article.</p>
<p><strong>As always, thank you for reading.</strong></p>
<p>Side-note. This Iris Black isn't intended to mirror the Iris Black in other MC&amp;D articles. She's my interpretation of the character - someone older, someone different. Marshall, Carter, and Black are all fantastic characters, but I can never seem to write within the lines of another authors narrative. That said, I whole heatedly encourage you to explore the <a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/marshall-carter-and-dark-hub">MC&amp;D Canon</a>, and the many fantastic articles and tales within.</p>
<p>Cheers!</p>
<hr />
