			<div class="content" id="post-content-4596698">
									

<p>Man, I <em>adore</em> this SCP. You've got this alien race that's dying of its own insensibility, and on the other hand there's MC&amp;D deriving twisted, hedonistic pleasure from that race's failure. It's existentially dreadful and filled with depravity on both ends. It's really impressive that you could tease that story out of <em>tapioca</em>, of all things.</p>
<p>The base anomaly was also interesting, and it had a really snappy description that was a pleasure to read. While I know other commenters found the transmissions excessive, I actually really love them. It shows how <em>desperate</em>, and more importantly how <em>petulant</em>, the SCP has become; so much of that characterisation would be lost if the messages weren't there. You'd basically be relying on Iris' monologue to characterise the SCP at that point.</p>
<p>Thanks for the read! This really made my day, and it's one of my favourites in Series 6 so far :)</p>
